Okay, so this is technically my second ascension (the other was also a
Neutral Gnomish Healer), but I wanted to wait until I got one on NAO
before posting here so that I could have a record proving it.  ;-)

I went for the protection racket, and got really lucky.  Usually my
strategy is to wander into the mines, search for a dwarf, wait for my
pet to kill it, and then take it=92s pick-axe;  then I return to the
Dungeons of Doom and look for vaults that I can mine to get enough
cash to purchase maximum protection.

However this time I instead ran into two bones files that greatly
accelerated this process.  The first one was in the first level of the
Mines, where I found a pick-axe immediately instead of having to hunt
down a dwarf with my pet.  Unfortunately pet-testing revealed it to be
cursed, but I figured that this didn=92t matter since I was going to be
a pacifist for a while anyway.  Ironically though, not too long after
wielding it I ran into my own bones file from a game I had just lost
20 minutes before!  So I didn=92t need the pick-axe after all, and
immediately got the cash I needed from my dead corpse instead.  :-)

I made it all the way to Minetown and then bought my protection.
There was a fountain nearby, but the guard yelled at me for using it,
so I waited for my pet to finish him off before making a serious
attempt to remove the curse from my pick-axe.  It took a few dips, but
I finally got my hands back.  This turned out to be the hardest part
of the early game;  from there I found and looted Sokoban and then
mined out the mines.  While I was there I got some helpful advice from
DarthL33tSA that helped me auto-identify the potions I found in the
Mine King=92s Cellar.

Some people consider healers to be a particularly difficult class with
which to ascend.  I however think that they are actually one of the
easier ones to ascend with if you have the protection racket.  One of
the reasons for this is because in the quest levels you there are lots
of dragon scales laying about just waiting to be turned into dragon
scale armor --- though you typically have to remove them from the
dragons that they are attached to first.  ;-)  And surely enough, when
I was done with my quest I not only had the Staff but also a brand new
set of gray dragon scale armor --- the perfect complement for my
amulet of reflection.

Not too long after this, though, I did something really stupid:  I put
an unidentified wand into my bag of holding and lost the bag in a
magical explosion.  In retrospect I am not sure whether this was
because I was sloppy in identifying the wand (I *thought* I=92d written
on the ground first before engraving with it to see if the writing
vanished, but maybe I forgot...) or whether it was because at the time
I hadn=92t realized that cursed wands always have a chance of making
your bag explode when you put them in.  Regardless, I was so
discouraged that I put the game down and walked away for a little over
a week.  Part of me wanted to give up entirely, but then I said to
myself, =93Dammit Greg, I am going to figure out a way to ascend this
healer!=94

I continued exploring the Dungeons of Doom in search of a new bag of
holding and even looted Fort Ludios without too much trouble thanks to
a cockatrice corpse I found on the floor right where a living one had
used to be standing ;-) --- actually the most annoying thing was that
I had to use my pick-axe to break apart something like 40 statues in
order to make sure I didn=92t miss any wands.  (Part of the reason I
used the cockatrice was because I wanted to stone several of the
soldiers as quickly as possible before they used up their wands.)

Anyway, sadly, there was no bag of holding so I continued all the way
down and stormed the Castle;  I crushed most of the really nasty
monsters in the drawbridge and then charged in to mop up the rest.  I
used my wand of wishing to get the Eyes of the Overworld and some
scrolls of genocide to wipe out Liches and Mind-flayers since I had
already received the The Eye of the Aethiopica from a magic lamp.

Why the Eyes of the Overworld, you may ask?  Because astral vision
makes exploring Hell a breeze!  It was still a little tedious, but at
least I didn=92t have to choose between utter boredom or using up
resources to write lots of scrolls of magic mapping.  The only
annoying thing was that since I didn=92t have a bag of holding, I had to
branchport back to Sokoban more often then I would have liked in order
to drop off the stuff that I was picking.  The surprising thing that I
discovered, though, was that you can really get by pretty well without
carrying a lot of stuff!

While I was exploring Hell, SmashFan2005 kept me company for while and
gave me a lot of useful advice (such as about cursed wands causing
bags to explode) for which I am grateful.  :-)

After a few levels I did finally run into a bag of holding (can=92t
remember where), which made life a LOT easier.  I wiped out Vlad and
Orcas --- though not before Orcas used all of the charges on his
wand.  :-/ Happily enough, the random number generator was kind to me
and not too long after I ran into two soldiers carrying more wands of
death, and one of the idiots killed himself after using just one
charge due to the reflected beam.  :-)

I cleared out the rest of Hell, and then finished assembling my
ascension kit.  The hard part was that I hadn=92t found any scrolls of
gold detection, which I needed to find the endgame portals.  I
considered using another wish, but instead I tried polypiling and out
of sheer luck manufactured a single scroll of gold detection, which
was enough for me to be able to make more with my magic marker.  After
this, since I was pretty well geared up, I didn=92t even bother to use
the last two wishes on my recharged wand, but instead kept them in
reserve.

I stormed the Wizard=92s Tower and got the Book of the Dead without too
much trouble, and then made my way down to the Sanctum.  There were so
many monsters there that there was only one thing for me to do:  use
my cockatrice corpse (which again just so happened to appear
conveniently on the floor in front of me right where a living
cockatrice used to be :-) ) to stone them all as well as the priests
of Mulloch.

The part that was really annoying, though, was that one of the
invisible level 5 demons started attacking me and summoning monsters,
and the same time Rodney appeared and made himself invisible so that
there were two =935=94=92s on my screen and it took me a while to realize
that one of them was Rodney since I had zapped him as soon as I saw
him and hadn=92t realized that he wasn=92t dead.  After not too long the
whole area was flooded with monsters and Rodney had stolen my Staff,
but when I finally figured out what was going on I zapped Rodney,
grabbed the Staff as well as the Amulet of Yendor, killed my way
through the crowd of monsters, and managed to run away from the
majority of them before they could catch up to me.

The mysterious force was incredibly unkind to me;  it felt at once
point like it was sending my back twice for every level it let me go
up.  I used up one and a half whole wands of death killing Rodneys and
had to recharge one of them;  at this point I was starting to get
worried that I would ever make it out of Hell alive.

That was the hardest part of the endgame.  After that, ascending the
Dungeon=92s of Doom was practically trivial, and most of the Elemental
Planes weren=92t too hard either, since I hard learned from watching the
tournament recordings on termcast.org that the key is to run as fast
as you can to the portals and not kill any monster that isn=92t getting
immediately in your way.  In the Plane of Earth I actually used my
wands of digging as much as possible in order to dig tunnels *around*
the monsters.

The Plane of Water was the worst, though, because the #%#$% portal
moved around so much that it took me forever to finally stumble into
it, and I had to use *three* scrolls of gold detection (I wrote two
more with my marker) in order to even have a clue of where it had
moved.

Finally, I was in the Astral Plane.  Since I had *two* wishes left in
my wand (not even including the =93wresting=94 wish), I wished for a
partially eaten chickatrice and mowed down everything between me and
the first altar;  I had to switch to the Staff to take out Death, but
oddly enough he turned out to be a wuss who fell after only a couple
of bashes.

I got REALLY lucky and the first altar turned out to be the right one,
so I immediately sacrificed the amulet and ascended.

Anyway, I am super excited to have pulled off ascending on a public
server!  :-D

